  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up the production of plant-based protein ingredients in India.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proeon Foods BV is based at the Delft Biotech Campus and is requesting a start-up loan of EUR 600k to expand their production site in Pune, India, for their plant-based protein ingredients being a healthy alternative to meat, dairy and eggs. Two of their products are now ready for commercial production: peanut protein and mung bean protein (see infographic below). International food companies use these products to replace, for example, chicken eggs which opens new commercial opportunities within the (vegan) food market.</narrative>
  </description>
